{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515796-personal-totems","id":515796,"title":"Personal Totems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-15T21:26:58-07:00","id":515796,"title":"Personal Totems","content":"Hello, forum! So, I'm hoping that one of you fellows can help me with a question I have re: the Totem merit in 2E. There are rules for creating Pack Totems, but there are no rules for creating personal totems. The Totem merit seems to imply, though, that Personal Totems are a thing and can happen:<br /> <br /> [quote']<br /> Effect: Your character has a relationship to a totem spirit,either personally or to a pack totem.<br /> [/quote]<br /> <br /> The problem that I'm having, though, is that per the Totem creation rules, this would have to start out at a minimum of 3 dots, since spirits are required to have at least a 1 in every attribute and Totem Points (i.e. merit dots) determines how many of those you get.<br /> <br /> So, even if you were to buy all 5 dots of this, you're still looking at a rank 1 spirit, and you couldn't start out with less than 3 dots to get a 1/1/1 spirit. That... seems pretty weak, especially for that much of an investment. The Familiar Tell from Wolf-Blooded gives you better than that, and you would be better off spending it on something like Mentor or True Friend.<br /> <br /> Was this intentional? Why mention personal totems if they're just going to be so weak as to be next to useless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T21:43:11-07:00","id":515819,"title":"","content":"The totem mechanics and merit seem to be for pack totems.<br /> <br /> The brief write up for the personal totem doesn't suggest that it offers you any mechanical benefits or is similar to a pack totem in anything but terminology. Until we get more books, it seems like Mentor would be a fine way to demonstrate it, with the spirit having its own attributes depending on its rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T21:55:23-07:00","id":515826,"title":"","content":"At Totem 5, you have a +5 bonus to Social actions with a Rank 1 spirit with an Essence capacity of 5, two Numina, a dot of Influences, a single Manifestation besides Twilight Form, and an Attribute spread of either 3/1/1 or 2/2/1, plus returning your investment slightly with the one Experience worth of totem boons and empowering rites. Totemic Empowerment and Totem Wrath are both viable uses of a simple totem for a solo character, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-16-2015, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T22:15:52-07:00","id":515831,"title":"","content":"What satchel said. I don't think a single Uratha would really be able to support a Totem more powerful than that on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T22:33:11-07:00","id":515835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515796-personal-totems?p=515831#post515831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What satchel said. I don't think a single Uratha would really be able to support a Totem more powerful than that on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e's greater focus on viably playable B-splats has me plugging this idea into a single Iron Master Elodoth running an investigation bureau full of Wolf-Blooded poking around Infrastructure and demonic interference. Toss that first Experience into a shared Alternate Identity and things get entertaining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T22:37:25-07:00","id":515837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515796-personal-totems?p=515835#post515835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2e's greater focus on viably playable B-splats has me plugging this idea into a single Iron Master Elodoth running an investigation bureau full of Wolf-Blooded poking around Infrastructure and demonic interference. Toss that first Experience into a shared Alternate Identity and things get entertaining.</div> </div> </div> </div>To make things interesting, I'd even rule Uratha can &quot;track&quot; (or sense) different covers thru having tasted the blood of one. Is it a compromise for the Unchained? yes, yes it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T22:42:43-07:00","id":515839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515796-personal-totems?p=515835#post515835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2e's greater focus on viably playable B-splats has me plugging this idea into a single Iron Master Elodoth running an investigation bureau full of Wolf-Blooded poking around Infrastructure and demonic interference. Toss that first Experience into a shared Alternate Identity and things get entertaining.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but like, all the Wolf-Blooded could take Pack Affinity and just buy more Totem dots to make a better Totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T22:59:56-07:00","id":515845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChanceTR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515796-personal-totems?p=515839#post515839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, but like, all the Wolf-Blooded could take Pack Affinity and just buy more Totem dots to make a better Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. All those mostly-NPC Wolf-Blooded. They sure have a say in how their dots get allocated and in no way have Totem capped at one dot as supporting characters.<br /> <br /> Pack Bond over the level of &quot;be able to purchase and contribute the cursory single Totem dot&quot; costs a third of your starting Merit dots on top of the Totem dots and the returns are slow and secondary to the benefits of having a network.<br /> <br /> This idea is orthogonal to your question. I'll gladly section it off into its own thread if the notion bothers you here, but stating the obvious offers no benefit in this situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T01:43:05-07:00","id":515946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515796-personal-totems?p=515845#post515845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. All those mostly-NPC Wolf-Blooded. They sure have a say in how their dots get allocated and in no way have Totem capped at one dot as supporting characters.<br /> <br /> Pack Bond over the level of &quot;be able to purchase and contribute the cursory single Totem dot&quot; costs a third of your starting Merit dots on top of the Totem dots and the returns are slow and secondary to the benefits of having a network.<br /> <br /> This idea is orthogonal to your question. I'll gladly section it off into its own thread if the notion bothers you here, but stating the obvious offers no benefit in this situation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, you're right. That was my bad. Apologies!<br /> <br /> I guess I could see how this would work out at 5 dots. They would offer some utility there. But what about at a lower level? The merit does technically go from 1-5 dots. At 3 dots, would the 1/1/1 spirit be comparable in utility to, say, a Mentor or an Ally at 3 dots? Or possibly taking a spirit as an ephemeral Retainer? Not all wolves have packs, and not all Wolf-Blooded have Uratha around to teach them the ins and outs of their nature. A lone wolf (or Wolf-Blooded) having access to a totem could be beneficial, if it's comparable at different ratings to something else they could buy.<br /> <br /> If not, what do you think could be done to make having an individual Totem at less than 4 or 5 dots a worthwhile investment? Should an individual Totem follow the same creation rules as a Pack totem, or possibly something more akin to what you might expect from a Mage Familiar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T04:29:11-07:00","id":516013,"title":"","content":"Well, at 1/1/1 we're talking 2 dice to most rolls, assuming we count that as rank 1. They could buff an attribute up to 4 if they had to, which puts their defense at 1-4, and most dice pools at 2-5 sans willpower, of which they have a 2 point pool. I guess if you spend their manifestation on reaching or fetter and their numina on telekinesis they'd be able to help in a few situations. Alternatively have them fetter to a doll or something and spend the numina on the possession manifestation. <br /> <br /> At 4 dots they can get a second numina that you can spend on another manifestation, which makes things a lot easier because getting unfetter means they can use the TK on something other than their host without risking running out of essence and being unable to reattach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T06:38:29-07:00","id":516131,"title":"","content":"Personal totems aren't really a thing in werewolf barring the lone wolf hack from the werewolf chroniclers guide.<br /> <br /> Outside of using lone wolf werewolves though, I'd say the only rule for personal totems that might not be unbalancing in a regular game is that someone with a personal totem isn't limited to five dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T06:55:09-07:00","id":516139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515796-personal-totems?p=516131#post516131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personal totems aren't really a thing in werewolf barring the lone wolf hack from the werewolf chroniclers guide.<br /> <br /> Outside of using lone wolf werewolves though, I'd say the only rule for personal totems that might not be unbalancing in a regular game is that someone with a personal totem isn't limited to five dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're implied to be a thing in at least one part of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T07:14:21-07:00","id":516176,"title":"","content":"I think the main reason the &quot;personal totem&quot; language is there is to support the &quot;Don't Say No&quot; Storyteller commandment. If someone really wanted to say &quot;Yeah, I'm contributing a dot to the Pack Totem, but I put half of the rest of my Merits into having my own side-totem&quot;, the ST can then say &quot;That's a weird idea but I see no problem with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> It might seem weird to have two totems, but in reality most Forsaken have at least four. By accepting their Auspice, Luna is their Totem. By being in a Tribe, the Firstborn patron of that Tribe is their Totem. By being in a Lodge, the guiding spirit of that Lodge is their Totem. By being in a Pack, the Pack Totem is their Totem. The three non-pack ones aren't supported mechanically because their Totem spirits are off the Rank 1-5 grid of things that are tracked with in-game mechanics. Plus, that would mean adding up the Totem points of hundreds and thousands of Werewolves the world over, and that's far more work than can be demanded of people. Again, not saying don't do it, just that it's a daunting task with questionable rewards. It might be a good way to work the Lodge-to-Tribe story, though...<br /> <br /> As to whether it balances out with other three to five dot Merits, I'd have to give that one a big Maybe. You get one Experience point back, so you could thereafter compare it to 2-4 point Merits. And what do you get for those sunk Experiences? You get a second character to control. As a totem for just you (the character), I'd say it's pretty invested in helping you (the character) along and thus you (the player) should control it. Sure, it's a relatively weak character, but it's also a relatively unique player character. With Totem's Wrath (which would be much easier to pull off with a weaker spirit; my pack's totem would contest with 15 dice, so that's never happening), your second character can sort-of enter Gauru form.<br /> You also get slapped with an annoying (and Beat granting) extra Rank 1 ban. Oh! And you get a bonus Aspiration slot.<br /> Overall, its a weird imvestment, but not a bad one.<br /> <br /> In response to StSword not limiting to 5 dots idea, I'd say that part of what shows that spirits grow as the network of fealty under them grows is that dot limitation. Now, were the Werewolf to have a Primal Urge above 5, thus raising the caps for things, that would be a slightyl different story. Typically, though, if you want a bigger personal totem, it would have to stop being personal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T08:09:22-07:00","id":516201,"title":"","content":"Actually is that 5-dot limit in total or per totem? <br /> <br /> Like, could you spend all 5 on one massive totem, and then buy another for yourself to represent being chummy with one of that spirit's underlings? <br /> <br /> Could a pack have 2 totems?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T08:56:47-07:00","id":516220,"title":"","content":"In my mind, Totem in Werewolf is analogous to Haunt in Geist (I'm even giving my players a free dot of Haunt in the Geist chronicle I just started), and therein you can contribute 5 dots each to several Haunts.<br /> <br /> While in theory there is no mechanical reason you shouldn't be able to have more than one, you have to ask yourself if you'd really want to. If you have two Pack Totems, they'll start competing with each other and pulling the pack in separate directions. Soon enough you'll basically end up with two packs. Or maybe you'll have a civil war. It'd make for some interesting stories either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T09:04:13-07:00","id":516227,"title":"","content":"TerraBen, Lodge totems mostly are in the Rank 1-5 scale (most of them being Rank 4, I think). But I agree with the rest of your argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T09:52:05-07:00","id":516252,"title":"","content":"Ah. I hadn't seen a write up for any of them and assumed they were typically Rank 6, with the Firstborn being Rank 7 and Luna being Rank 8.<br /> <br /> Even Rank 4 is off the scale of benefits given on page 92. The best row from that is &quot;20+&quot;, and Rank 4 doesn't start until 26. A pack of 4 Uratha (my pack's size) that are highly dedicated to their totem and supported by a decent number of Wolf-Blooded could get there, I suppose. That said, I imagine people are more dedicated to their Pack than they are to their lodge.<br /> Plus there's a lot more info to come on Lodges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T10:55:24-07:00","id":516324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515796-personal-totems?p=516252#post516252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus there's a lot more info to come on Lodges.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that the normal rank of Lodge Totems will change in Second Edition, but we'll know that when we get more info. But I think that while a Rank 6 spirit could be willing to become a Tribal Totem of a large Tribe, they would probably think it beneath them to tend to a Lodge. Mostly because most Lodges only have hundreds of members at most, while Tribes could have tens of thousands. Why would a spirit &quot;god&quot; care about a hundred people? Of course, there are always exceptions.<br /> <br /> (BTW, my source for Lodge Totem Ranks is Lodges of the Faithful, on page 25, where it notes that most Lodge Totems are Rank 4, and some are Rank 5.)<br /> <br /> As a somewhat more on topic comment, maybe we will get some more totem options (including personal totems) in the next book, The Pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T11:09:38-07:00","id":516354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515796-personal-totems?p=516252#post516252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus there's a lot more info to come on Lodges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T23:32:07-07:00","id":516794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515796-personal-totems?p=516201#post516201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually is that 5-dot limit in total or per totem?<br /> <br /> Like, could you spend all 5 on one massive totem, and then buy another for yourself to represent being chummy with one of that spirit's underlings?<br /> <br /> Could a pack have 2 totems?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They might very well change things in second edition, but in first edition a werewolf it didn't seem like a werewolf could have more than one pack totem connection at a time. <br /> <br /> As evidenced by the rules for crusades in war against the pure, when the crusaders form new packs with a crusade sponsoring spirits they are no longer a part of their former packs, for as long as the crusade lasts.<br /> <br /> If one could collect totems, it would be a lot easier to just take existing packs, get them new temporary pack totems for the crusade, and let the benefits accumulate, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T03:27:38-07:00","id":516914,"title":"","content":"I figure that might be more to do with spirit politics than any sort of metaphysical limit though. I think if you got a couple of spirits willing to enter a joint-totem partnership they could probably do it.<br /> <br /> Actually thinking about it the whole &quot;everybody gets the benefits regardless of whether they contributed to the totem point pot&quot; thing might be a justification for letting players get more bang for their buck on personal totems. A pack totem is spreading itself a bit thin by lending it's power to everyone, whereas a personal totem is only connected to one person. It's a more intimate link.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't triple the effectiveness though. The chronicler's guide did that in order to make one person get the benefits they would have done in a pack, so it would be overkill here. Not to mention it would make any odd-point totem effectively free. Maybe a smaller boost, to get it in the range of a familiar though? Maybe doubled? Or half-again? And if we do that we can probably drop the one experience you get back because lets face it there's no real difference between that and a discount on the totem itself if you're the only one getting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T18:51:47-07:00","id":517524,"title":"","content":"On the note of lodge totems and their power, scarred bear was so strong the firstborn could not take him out. I dont see him being so far below the firstborn in that case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T20:30:00-07:00","id":525040,"title":"","content":"Considering it's possible, not too likely, but possible, for a pack to have a level five spirit as a totem, it would make sense that lodge totems might be in archspirit levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}